  data: {
    LLM: "Game: Swingo Poker. Blinds, three betting rounds, best five from seven cards (two hole, three board, river, one from another's board). Pot limit.",
    Player: "Poker with blinds and pot-limit betting. Choose two hole and three board cards; use river and one other player's board card at showdown.",
    objective: "Win the pot by making the best five-card poker hand from seven cards: your two hole cards, your three board cards, the shared river card, and any one exposed card from another player's board.",
    gameplay: "After the deal and first betting round, each player chooses two hole cards (hidden) and three board cards (exposed). All expose their boards; second betting round, started by the highest board. Dealer deals one shared river card to the center; third betting round, again started by highest board. Showdown: each player makes the best five-card hand from their two hole cards, three board cards, river card, and one card from any other player's board. Best hand wins; ties split the pot.",
    keyRules: [
      "Blinds (small and big) are posted before the deal by the two players to dealer's left.",
      'First betting round is started by the player left of the big blind.',
      'Each player must choose two hole cards and three board cards; boards are exposed simultaneously.',
      'Second and third betting rounds are started by the surviving player with the highest ranking set of board cards (pairs, two pair, trips count; incomplete straights and flushes do not).',
      'A player may only fold when facing a bet or raise they are unwilling to call; if already matching the current bet they cannot fold (others may need their board card).',
      "At showdown each player may use any five of their seven available cards; the river and another player's board card are optional.",
      "Board cards of folded players are mucked face down; surviving players' board cards remain visible for others to use.",
    ],
